nkedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T05:18:02-07:00","id":1247994,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UW8vRvGvCKs\" target=\"_blank\">Rian Johnson's Trilogy - Canceled</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-20-2018, 08:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T12:06:35-07:00","id":1248160,"title":"","content":"There's a whole lot of speculation going around there.<br /> <br /> Whatever project is even being discussed in the actual quote by Lamont can't even said to be cancelled, just facing development problems.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T19:54:07-07:00","id":1248278,"title":"","content":"I finally got out the barf bucket and roll of paper towels, and opened up my window in case I needed a &quot;NOPE&quot; emergency exit, and forced myself to watch it for the first time tonight, already familiar with the arguments for and against, and basically the plot of the entire movie.<br /> <br /> My takeaway was it was just...dumb. Not good, not bad, just...dumb. It was just so milquetoast and middling of a movie I can't even find space for strong feelings on it. In some ways it was better than people give it credit for, others way, <i>way </i>worse. The one thing I can definitively say, is the people who defend it because it &quot;subverts expectations&quot;, or attack critics because they didn't understand Star Wars or the film, are weapons-grade nutters. Basically the beginning and end of any real criticism I can care enough about to cobble together, is the plot and action of the movie contradict its core themes and commentary on the most fundamental levels.<br /> <br /> And, I say that as someone completely on board with the movie on the conceptual and thematic level. My favorite piece of Star Wars fiction to this day is KotOR2, precisely because it intelligently deconstructs and critiques the nature of good and evil, right and wrong, within the context of the Star Wars universe, and the role of the Jedi and Sith in relation to those concepts of good and evil. Honestly, if I could express one strong emotion about the movie, it's disappointment Johnson couldn't bring that deconstruction and the themes he clearly felt important home, by writing a screenplay consistent with its own internal logic.<br /> <br /> To use a baseball metaphor...in the OT, Lucas swung for the bleachers and hit two home runs and an infield pop fly triple. The PT was two foul balls and a single. Abrams bunted with TFA, but in TLJ Johnson swung for the fucking parking lot but spun out on the plate and hit the umpire in the face.<br /> <br /> There is a single shot in the movie I can point to as pretty much the capstone of how tone-deaf, contradictory, and self-defeating the film is. &quot;We don't fight to destroy what we hate, we fight to save what we love!&quot;...while the siege laser is actually firing in the background, <i>and it's the focal point of the shot</i>. When, you know, the entire point of Finn's story arc in TLJ was that after a moment of weakness, Finn experienced the callousness and cruelty that led him to defect from the First Order in the first place from a different perspective, experienced betrayal, found his reasons to fight again, and in the end was about to sacrifice himself...to <i>save the people he loved</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 08-20-2018, 11:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-21T04:14:17-07:00","id":1248378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1248160#post1248160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a whole lot of speculation going around there.<br /> <br /> Whatever project is even being discussed in the actual quote by Lamont can't even said to be cancelled, just facing development problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, Star Wars YouTubers love to speculate and rile people up(Except for Star Wars Explained, that channel is great and the guy who does it is really nice). So, I'll wait for an official announcement from Disney.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":24,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","user":"Mr Gone","date":". 08-21-2018, 07:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-21T05:30:15-07:00","id":1248393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1248278#post1248278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My favorite piece of Star Wars fiction to this day is KotOR2, precisely because it intelligently deconstructs and critiques the nature of good and evil, right and wrong, within the context of the Star Wars universe, and the role of the Jedi and Sith in relation to those concepts of good and evil.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree, KOTOR2 did a good job of portraying why the Jedi philosophy is flawed. By seeing the world in terms of black and white, they lost touch with the people they were supposed to be protecting, and that lead to the people losing faith in them, which enabled the Sith to get a foothold in Republic territory.<br /> <br /> Just a shame that the meatbags in charge of producing the game never got around to finishing it before release. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-21T08:01:30-07:00","id":1248415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1248378#post1248378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yea, Star Wars YouTubers love to speculate and rile people up(Except for Star Wars Explained, that channel is great and the guy who does it is really nice). So, I'll wait for an official announcement from Disney.</div> </div> </div> </div>I used to really like Thor Skywalker before his channel became nothing but him complaining about TLJ. His theories were really down to earth and he even predicted Rey\u2019s parents being no one important. But unfortunately, he can\u2019t seem to let go of his disappointment with TLJ and it\u2019s all he talks about any more. Like, fine, you didn\u2019t like the movie. Sorry you felt that way, but do you have to keep dwelling on it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-21T09:22:10-07:00","id":1248429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1248393#post1248393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree, KOTOR2 did a good job of portraying why the Jedi philosophy is flawed. By seeing the world in terms of black and white, they lost touch with the people they were supposed to be protecting, and that lead to the people losing faith in them, which enabled the Sith to get a foothold in Republic territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my mind it's not even that, it's the question of how does one handle morally grey actors in a universe where good and evil are truly objective and externally enforced by a phenomenon intrinsic and necessary to the established universe. It even hints at the question of whether or not Force-sensitive individuals have, or are capable of, free will. Relative to the role of the Force in TLJ, Johnson seems to be taking a &quot;yay Potentium!&quot; view (even though he, or probably most people outside Lucasfilm Animation*, probably has no idea what that is), but in the context of the Star Wars universe, it just doesn't work. His own film disproves his thesis.<br /> <br /> Luke sabers up against Ben and realizes what he's doing, but it's too late. Any Star Wars fan is going to read that as Luke being tempted by the Dark Side, <i>again</i>, which was the catalyst for Ben to embrace the Dark Side. Ben is pushed into increasingly heinous acts by Snooki, each one he believes to be the one that will allow him to cross the threshold and become consumed by the Dark Side, but he's conflicted as his acts were the consequence of Hobson's choices forced upon him by Snooki.<br /> <br /> Along comes Rey, and she whoops his ass in a scene every fan who knows their SW lore walked out of the theater saying &quot;she was calling on the Dark Side to beat him&quot;. Hell, the novelization made it clear. Even three years ago when the dipshits on the internet were like &quot;buh how Rey swang litesabur guder&quot;, I was there to say &quot;she was calling on the Dark Side, dipshit. Pay attention to the movie.&quot; Even then, the point was being laid out Kylo is weak because calling on the Dark Side doesn't come naturally to him, whereas Rey is a natural at it.<br /> <br /> That's why of all the theories about Rey's parentage, I preferred &quot;she's either a kid or a Rule 63 clone of Palpatine&quot;.<br /> <br /> Enter TLJ, and Snooki's up to his usual bullshit with Kylo, while Luke goes from &quot;the Jedi Order is shit and I won't teach you&quot; to &quot;you're a Dark-sider, fuck off&quot;. Rey's tempted to go to Kylo and try to redeem him, but it was dead obvious from the beginning she was being tempted by the Dark side. She goes to Kylo, Kylo whacks Snooki -- this being the point he embraces the Dark Side, having made the deliberate choice of his own volition to betray and murder his own master -- and one terribly choreographed fight scene later we're expected to buy Rey has turned her back on the Dark Side because she thinks Kylo is a dick.<br /> <br /> The only actually clear, consistent message any of this presents, is &quot;Dark Jedi can do good things, too&quot;. Well, no shit, Sherlock. The entire point is the road to Hell is paved with good intentions. Plagueis, if I remember right, wanted for no one to suffer the pain and loss of loved ones' deaths. Maul wanted to preserve and honor his culture. Count Dookie wanted to purge the Jedi Order and Republic of corruption and stagnancy and return them to their former grandeur. Anakin wanted to save Padme and their children. Ben wanted to live up to the crushing weight of his family's legacy. As far as the canon characters, Palpatine was the only Dark-sider with purely malicious intent from beginning to end.<br /> <br /> The kill-shot on Johnson's one consistent thesis, even separating the &quot;road to hell&quot; aspect, is there's absolutely nothing innovative or subversive there. Even constraining our frame of reference to the cinematic part of the universe, we've already seen a character who calls on the Dark Side to do right, but does not become consumed by it: Mace Windu. And, expanding that frame of reference to the CG series', Ventress (at least, after the Nightsister genocide) is our case example for a character who is unambiguously, unrepentantly dark, but (sometimes?) turns her power to achieve benevolent ends.<br /> <br /> What's the logical progression from this one should expect in Episode IX, based on two entire movies of characterization of Rey and Kylo, and be in any way whatsoever internally consistent? Kylo sits around being emo while the First Order consolidates rule over the galaxy, and decides maybe being an evil despot isn't the best way to pass his time just for Rey to show up, kill him and seize power, and declare herself the next Sith lord, that's where. You know, so those kids at the end of Episode VIII can grow up to fight Darth Rey or what the fuck ever money teat Disney plans to brutalize next.<br /> <br /> <i>[Let's be honest with ourselves for a minute. Lucasfilm Animation is obviously the Star Wars nerd containment zone within the company as a whole.]</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-21T10:10:15-07:00","id":1248448,"title":"","content":"That's a nice take on it, I've been seeing it a little differently<br /> <br /> First we see (1-3), forced good brings stagnation and they was balance, but they really aren't part of that true balance, (4-6) putting evil or tyranny in control (may allow growth of society) doesn't bring enlightenment)<br /> <br /> I, for my own sanity here, imagine that the real story is let the people be themselves, sure we need administrative structures, but they can never really help the people themselves philosophically<br /> <br /> I feel more like Loki or a fairly good version of Nyarlathotep came along and gave us the Jedi and the Sith and then set back to watch if we're screw things up with both good and evil fighting for balance, or if we've see the bigger picture, get the joke, and never have good or evil in real control, but just work together and/or live and let live, in a way to bring and provide some means of prosperity for everyone","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24473-willowfang","name":"Willowfang","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24473_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-21T10:14:37-07:00","id":1248450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1248393#post1248393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a shame that the meatbags in charge of producing the game never got around to finishing it before release. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's a shame Lucasfilm made them release it about 6 months before it was ready, because they wanted it to coincide with the release of Episode III. I think KotOR 2 would have been absolutely fantastic if it had gotten the time necessary to polish it and bring everything together. Instead it was merely just really, really good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-21T10:25:47-07:00","id":1248453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1248429#post1248429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">one terribly choreographed fight scene</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a rather distinct opinion.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-21T11:01:26-07:00","id":1248461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Willowfang</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1248448#post1248448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and never have good or evil in real control, but just work together and/or live and let live, in a way to bring and provide some means of prosperity for everyone</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference between the Sith and Jedi isn't so much good and evil but rather Selfishness and Selflessness. The Sith are inherently selfish and do whatever they want and who cares about other people. The Jedi are inherently selfless to the point that putting their own desires first goes against the basic tenants of the Order. <br /> <br /> And honestly I don't know that you really can &quot;live and let live&quot; with the Sith. Their entire philosophy is basically, &quot;Strong people can do whatever they want and weak people just have to deal with it, or become strong enough to force the other guy to stop.&quot; At the very least, I don't know that I'd want to be neighbors with a guy who sincerely believed that and had magical mind control powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-21T11:09:44-07:00","id":1248464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1248453#post1248453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a rather distinct opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's actually not. It's objective fact, and I can prove it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/fyIPvIjVMYo?t=1m42s\" data-code=\"fyIPvIjVMYo\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/fyIPvIjVMYo/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> At the beginning of the fight -- approximately 1:45 into the linked video -- one of the Praetorian Guard actors takes a swing straight at Daisy Ridley's neck. She missed her cue to duck, and the actor had to stop his swing and deflect upwards to avoid conking her in the back of the head with the prop. This is after this specific actor comes from behind camera, blocking the focal point of the shot -- Ridley and Driver -- dives and spins for no real reason, blocking the focal point of the shot while also breaking the actor's line of sight which was already compromised by the costume, while Ridley's attention was focused elsewhere, putting him in the position to hit her in the back of the head in the first place. This all occurs in the immediate foreground, center-frame.<br /> <br /> There's another shot at about 3:20 where the dual-wielding Praetorian actually stabs Ridley in the back with one of his props while arm locking her, and she visibly reacts to being stabbed in the back with a prop on screen. They had to CG edit the Praetorian's second dagger completely out in post.<br /> <br /> Once you see it there's no going back. It's some real Star Wars Kid shit. That is not good fight choreography.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 08-21-2018, 02:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-21T11:43:10-07:00","id":1248476,"title":"","content":"That sure is an... interesting take on the film, and on Star Wars in general. That's very much not how I read it, but hey, we all interpret media through our own experiences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-21T12:01:26-07:00","id":1248478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1248464#post1248464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the beginning of the fight -- approximately 1:45 into the linked video -- one of the Praetorian Guard actors takes a swing straight at Daisy Ridley's neck. She missed her cue to duck, and the actor had to stop his swing and deflect upwards to avoid conking her in the back of the head with the prop. This is after this specific actor comes from behind camera, blocking the focal point of the shot -- Ridley and Driver -- dives and spins for no real reason, blocking the focal point of the shot while also breaking the actor's line of sight which was already compromised by the costume, while Ridley's attention was focused elsewhere, putting him in the position to hit her in the back of the head in the first place. This all occurs in the immediate foreground, center-frame.<br /> <br /> There's another shot at about 3:20 where the dual-wielding Praetorian actually stabs Ridley in the back with one of his props while arm locking her, and she visibly reacts to being stabbed in the back with a prop on screen. They had to CG edit the Praetorian's second dagger completely out in post.</div> </div> </div> </div>Citation for this, considering you put up the clip of the actual fight, and not a behind-the-scenes featurette?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That is not good fight choreography. </div> </div> </div>I've seen bad fight choreography. This ain't it.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://img1.ak.crunchyroll.com/i/spire2/b6c595d8aaccf60ead24fdb0be4ff5f01507232105_full.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-21T12:04:04-07:00","id":1248479,"title":"","content":"QUOTE=Isator Levi;n1248453]<br /> <br /> That's a rather distinct opinion.<br /> [/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> It was pretty bad on a technical level, not opinion. You would expect professional level quality actors, choreography, and editing from a movie with this kind of budget and yet not only does it look like everyone is just dancing around each other or bumbling around like power ranger villain henchmen but you have a weapon prop disappearing from a guards hand mid fight in a pretty important scene. A believable fight scene doesn't have to sacrifice how visually entertaining it is but it certainly requires more talent.<br /> All in all, the fight is flashy, sure. But it lacks substance and any sense of danger which leaves the whole scene looking like filler.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7108-satcom","name":"Satcom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-21T13:30:58-07:00","id":1248495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1248429#post1248429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> snip</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of calling on the dark side to accomplish good things, I thought that's what the Shadow Jedi were all about? They combine the powers of Light and Dark, thus creating Shadow.<br /> <br /> Or am I mistaken about that? Because I don't think we've actually seen the Shadow Jedi make an appearance in the cinematic universe, yet?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1248464#post1248464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/fyIPvIjVMYo?t=1m42s\" data-code=\"fyIPvIjVMYo\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/fyIPvIjVMYo/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the whole purpose of the Praetorian armor was that it was resistant to lightsaber blades and strengthened the wearer's connection to the dark side by keeping them in a perpetual state of agony?<br /> <br /> Also, that is a lot of battle cries for somebody who's supposedly turned their back on the dark side. Even Kylo isn't screaming that much!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-21-2018, 04:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-21T16:03:07-07:00","id":1248546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1248415#post1248415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I used to really like Thor Skywalker before his channel became nothing but him complaining about TLJ. His theories were really down to earth and he even predicted Rey\u2019s parents being no one important. But unfortunately, he can\u2019t seem to let go of his disappointment with TLJ and it\u2019s all he talks about any more. Like, fine, you didn\u2019t like the movie. Sorry you felt that way, but do you have to keep dwelling on it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel the same way about the channel Star Wars Theory. It used to be fun, but then he just started downing on TLJ and such. I got sick of it so I unsubscribed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divid