iv class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satcom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1249770#post1249770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not that I'm aware of.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. Just a guess, as I saw a very similar critique of the same scene there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T09:39:12-07:00","id":1250470,"title":"","content":"I'm just going to throw my .02 in here. I saw TLJ and I...nothing the movie I guess. Let me explain. I grew up in the 90s, so the Original Series what it until I was out of high school. I actually liked the prequels, so there's that. But until TFA showed up, I was deep into the Expanded Universe. I read almost all the books, played the video and tabletop games, and generally considered it the history of what happened after Episode VI. So when TFA came out, I thought it was cool, but for me it wasn't what &quot;really&quot; happened. I liked it, but it didn't hit all the emotional notes the old EU did for me.<br /> TLJ was a good movie in an objective sense. Good direction, great acting, etc. I didn't particularly like what they did with the story, but I understand why certain choices were made. I don't particularly like those choices when compared with what happened in, say, the Thrawn Trilogy, or the Fate of the Jedi for later books, but that's ok.<br /> I loved Rogue One, am excited to finally see Solo, and am 100% ambivalent for Ep 9. It just isn't MY Star Wars, as I understand it, and that's ok. I don't have to like the movies. I wish I did, and honestly it makes me really sad that I don't like TLJ because I have waited for so darn long for more movies, but I can live with it.<br /> As an aside, I think the decision to have Rey's parents be no one special is a good one. One of the big strengths of the Expanded Universe was the introduction of non-Solo/Skywalker Jedi characters. Didn't detract from the main characters at all, but added to the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T14:58:19-07:00","id":1250540,"title":"","content":"/<br /> <br /> I, for a long time, absolutely despised the prequels ... then, &quot;The Last Jedi&quot; was released.<br /> <br /> Now, looking back, I have a new found appreciation for the prequel trilogy. It has character &amp; story continuity. Even though some of the story was juvenile in its approach, it was uniform and fit the basic novelle. As many mistakes as Lucas made with these movies, I would rather have his storytelling than the current disillusioned franchise.<br /> <br /> It hit me how unoriginal the Disney SW movies are even to the point where they couldn\u2019t even change the design of ships 30 years later after ROTJ as Xwings and Star Destroyer have not evolved with technology? Lucas at least gave us that, and took the time to show how technology changed from Episode 1 to Episode 4.<br /> <br /> I went back and have a new appreciation for the story Lucas was telling in the Prequel Trilogy as it was original and the overall arc tied into the Original Trilogy to make a consistent 1-6 narrative.<br /> <br /> Where Lucas went wrong was writing, directing and doing everything as he should have been more collaborative like the OT, because the execution is the real problem with the PT.<br /> <br /> The Storytelling in these new films is just some retread of the OT with a few left turns to make us feel like its original. Snoke dies in part 2 instead part 3, so now it\u2019s supposed to be genius writing! There is no theme to this Trilogy that ties with 1-6 as I still don\u2019t know what the point is and why it\u2019s called 7-9?<br /> <br /> Johnson's pitch to Kennedy was that he was going to tell a whole New Story, one where they introduced new characters and places.<br /> <br /> If you are creating a Whole New Story, then this is Not a continuation of the Original Story Line. The current strand of movies, should not be considered 7-9, Rather, 1, 2 &amp; 3 of a Story that takes place in the Star Wars Theme. Especially when information came out that Johnson was intending to spread this story into A New Galaxy. ??? Why go extramural Galaxy, when there are so many places there within the already developed Galaxy yet to see?<br /> <br /> So, here is a video clip of Rian Johnson which pretty much sums up what everyone has been saying about him <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2Fbtat5iPm4\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2Fbtat5iPm4</a><br /> <br /> Yes, he proves that by not knowing the source information enough to formulate a logical direction.<br /> <br /> Then there has been the question as to why make Luke some Curmudgeon on an uncharted isolated planet.<br /> <br /> I'll tell you exactly why they made Luke the hermit on a remote planet island ... Lazy as F*ck Storytelling.<br /> <br /> Just like &quot;The Force Awakens&quot; &quot;The Last Jedi&quot; told a completely unoriginal tale. Rian Johnson simply ripped off more Story context from the original trilogy.<br /> <br /> Think of when Luke went to find Ben Kenobi [Obi-Wan]:<br /> --- He was a hermit [\u2714]<br /> <br /> --- He failed at teaching the most powerfully gifted inherent Force adept in the galaxy [\u2714]<br /> <br /> --- His Star pupil murdered all of the students in Jedi training while turning to the Dark Side [\u2714]<br /> <br /> --- The now former Star pupil is the apprentice to &amp; strong arm of the Dark Sith Lord who leads the galaxy wide military that seeks out and slaughters all who would raise up against them [\u2714]<br /> <br /> --- His former Star Pupil now Crusader for the Dark Side killed his Sith Lord Master to save the protagonist of the movie [\u2714]<br /> <br /> Now think of when Luke went to seek out Yoda:<br /> <br /> --- Yoda lived on a remote Planet no one ever goes to [\u2714]<br /> <br /> --- Yoda was stubborn and did not want to teach Luke the ways of being a Jedi [\u2714]<br /> <br /> --- Yoda eventually gave in to teach Luke how to focus his Force abilities [\u2714]<br /> <br /> --- The hero ran off without finishing his training to help friends in danger [\u2714]<br /> <br /> Nothing about this series is creative or original. These first two Disney Star Wars flicks are a simple poor retelling of Star Wars episodes IV V &amp; VI ... and the only thing new they added, were in your face real world ideologies, that were implanted to force politics into the movies.<br /> <br /> I do not want to think about what is happening in real world society when I go to see a Space Fantasy designated in a Galaxy Far Far Away. I come to see these movies to take me away from the real world, as an escape for a couple of hours.<br /> <br /> If you're going to force your politics in my face, wait until the premiere, and have your cast voice their opinions [which are scripted and really your opinions] on the Red Carpet during the interview as they enter the theater.<br /> <br /> Putting this into a movie that already has its own political upheaval, simply makes no sense whatsoever.<br /> <br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6040-quiet-storm","name":"Quiet Storm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T15:11:29-07:00","id":1250544,"title":"","content":"It's always been the case with Star Wars, due to it's enormous popularity, that the movies have never quite matched what fans think inside their own heads about the quality or integrity of the stories involved. If you look at the series as a whole, it's desperately inconsistent and unlike other franchises it doesn't have another medium source (like literature or comics) to fall back on in case the movie doesn't work out.<br /> <br /> For the record, I actually liked large parts of The Last Jedi - in my view, Luke Skywalker has never been presented in such a human and yet, by the end, really cool way. However, my favourite Star Wars movies are the original and Rogue One, fundamentally because they were self contained stories that didn't require you to watch and essentially adulate the series as a whole. For fanboy movies, I'll probably prefer Dune a lot more when it comes out in a few years time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 09-02-2018, 05:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T16:51:42-07:00","id":1250569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChewyGranola</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1250470#post1250470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It just isn't MY Star Wars, as I understand it, and that's ok. I don't have to like the movies</div> </div> </div> </div>I wish more people thought the way you do. Thanks for saying...<br /> <br /> Sorry it wasn't for you, but I'm glad you're not trashing all things star wars just because you personally didn't like it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T17:00:08-07:00","id":1250571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quiet Storm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1250540#post1250540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It hit me how unoriginal the Disney SW movies are even to the point where they couldn\u2019t even change the design of ships 30 years later after ROTJ as Xwings and Star Destroyer have not evolved with technology? Lucas at least gave us that, and took the time to show how technology changed from Episode 1 to Episode 4.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ok, I have to comment on this.<br /> <br /> One, in the old EU, the Star Wars universe was technologically stagnant. They'd had hyperdrive technology for thousands of a years. Why in 30 years would technology need to advance? Especially under the rule of the Empire? 30 years in a spacefairing society is nothing. Why wouldn't the same ships still be in use? Granted, that was the old EU, but I'd still think in the new cannon that idea that Galaxy is technological stagnant still holds true.<br /> <br /> To that point, and for a real world equivalent, this video summed it up nicely:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=p4zU-90QbvE\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=p4zU-90QbvE\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=p4zU-90QbvE\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=p4zU-90QbvE </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-02T00:03:27-07:00","id":1250675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1250544#post1250544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, my favourite Star Wars movies are the original and Rogue One, fundamentally because they were self contained stories that didn't require you to watch and essentially adulate the series as a whole.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, me too! I mean, I still rank ESB and RotJ over Rogue One because the original trilogy is a great self-contained story in three parts, but it\u2019s definitely my favorite outside the originals.<br /> <br /> I think <s>Star Wars</s> A New Hope was a fantastic standalone story, and Empire and Jedi were an unplanned two-part sequel that miraculously turned out well for once. The prequels did what prequels do and made the overall story weaker by adding a bunch of unnecessary context to a story that was just fine without it. The 4, 5, 2, 3, 6 viewing order kinda sorta works by reframing Anakin\u2019s story as part of Luke\u2019s instead of its own, but the execution just isn\u2019t quite there. TFA was eh, same story as New Hope again, but this time with as much nostalgia pandering as they could squeeze in and a side-helping of Abrams mystery box, but I forgave it because I knew Disney had to do everything they could to endear themselves to the fans after the buyout. Then Rogue One was, while not a perfect move, the best since the original trilogy. And The Last Jedi, while also not perfect, did it\u2019s damnedest to let the past die (killing it, if it had to) in hopes that we might finally get a new damn story in this universe that isn\u2019t completely defined by its relationship to the original trilogy. Hopefully we get it once they finish this trilogy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-02T06:49:33-07:00","id":1250733,"title":"","content":"I think the best thing for Star Wars would be to let it fall into the public domain. Let literally anyone cook up a Star Wars short story, movie, novel, video game, et cetera.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-02T08:11:58-07:00","id":1250751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1250733#post1250733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the best thing for Star Wars would be to let it fall into the public domain. Let literally anyone cook up a Star Wars short story, movie, novel, video game, et cetera.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly I think that's true for many franchises.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-02T11:00:26-07:00","id":1250810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1250751#post1250751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I think that's true for many franchises.</div> </div> </div> </div>Imagine if anyone who wanted to could do a Batman or Superman movie of their own. I mean, yeah, sure, we still probably would've gotten a turd as loathsome as <i>Dawn of Justice</i>, but there'd've been a chance at a few gems that year, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-02T14:07:57-07:00","id":1250840,"title":"","content":"I'm... not that confident.<br /> <br /> I think in most mediums, going public domain generally works for a franchise, but comics, prose, even theatre, and such are much smaller endeavors. Films, especially feature length films, have a very bad history with public domain properties, that seems fairly linked to the sheer size of production necessary.<br /> <br /> The history of public domain properties in films is consistently lots and lots of turds for every OK movie, and then lots of those for anything you can consider a gem.<br /> <br /> There are ~200 Dracula movies out there (obviously you run into some counting issues based on a number of factors)... how many of them are gems? Not a lot.<br /> <br /> Going public domain also isn't going to address the, &quot;Not my [Franchise]&quot; phenomenon even when handled maturely. It just gives more things for people to argue about. As someone like ChewyGranola, the EU was &quot;my Star Wars,&quot; but even then there was a lot of fandom arguments (esp. once the Internet got more popular) about various EU works such as the earlier books that aren't that consistent with canon and the rest of the EU (*cough* Splinter of the Mind's Eye *cough*), and whether certain novels should be discarded because the author &quot;didn't get Star Wars.&quot; Tossing all the Star Wars fan fic into the mix and having to sort the wheat from the chaff doesn't seem like a recipe for franchise health; even if a few good novels or comics might have been made that otherwise wouldn't (within the Star Wars universe, since some people just make their own setting and all that).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-02T22:22:48-07:00","id":1250974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1250840#post1250840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The history of public domain properties in films is consistently lots and lots of turds for every OK movie, and then lots of those for anything you can consider a gem.</div> </div> </div> </div>...like the somewhat more recent glut of Robin Hood and King Arthur adaptations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-02T22:53:36-07:00","id":1250977,"title":"","content":"I wonder if the 'everyone involved with this horrible movie should die in a fire' crowd would give up or just be spread a little thin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-02T23:23:23-07:00","id":1250981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1250840#post1250840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Films, especially feature length films, have a very bad history with public domain properties, that seems fairly linked to the sheer size of production necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, it's not like anyone watched or enjoyed Snow White, Sleeping Beauty, Fantasia, Cinderella, Pinocchio, the Little Mermaid, Beauty and the Beast, Aladdin, Alice in Wonderland, Around the World in 80 Days, Atlantis, A Bug's Life, Chicken Little, A Christmas Carol, Frozen, Hercules, John Carter, Mulan, the Princess and the Frog, Tangled, Tarzan, The Adventures of Ichabod and Mr. Toad, the Jungle Book, the Three Musketeers, the Sword in the Stone, Treasure Planet, or Muppet Treasure Island.<br /> <br /> \u200bDisney has consistently proven that the public domain can be a great source of cinematic inspiration. It's actually rather frustrating that they've strangled it so thoroughly after exploiting it so consistently.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1250840#post1250840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The history of public domain properties in films is consistently lots and lots of turds for every OK movie, and then lots of those for anything you can consider a gem.<br /> <br /> There are ~200 Dracula movies out there (obviously you run into some counting issues based on a number of factors)... how many of them are gems? Not a lot.<br /> <br /> Going public domain also isn't going to address the, &quot;Not my [Franchise]&quot; phenomenon even when handled maturely. It just gives more things for people to argue about. As someone like ChewyGranola, the EU was &quot;my Star Wars,&quot; but even then there was a lot of fandom arguments (esp. once the Internet got more popular) about various EU works such as the earlier books that aren't that consistent with canon and the rest of the EU (*cough* Splinter of the Mind's Eye *cough*), and whether certain novels should be discarded because the author &quot;didn't get Star Wars.&quot; Tossing all the Star Wars fan fic into the mix and having to sort the wheat from the chaff doesn't seem like a recipe for franchise health; even if a few good novels or comics might have been made that otherwise wouldn't (within the Star Wars universe, since some people just make their own setting and all that).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the sheer dearth we have of stuff that's been added to the public domain in recent years (thanks in no small part to Disney pushing for the laws about when things can the public domain being changed) makes these kinds of assumptions a bit iffy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 09-03-2018, 02:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-03T01:03:57-07:00","id":1250996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1250974#post1250974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...like the somewhat more recent glut of Robin Hood and King Arthur adaptations?</div> </div> </div> </div>Among others, yes. Some of them are fun however much they're not good movies though. Though that's why I phrased it as &quot;turd, OK, and gem,&quot; since lots of people enjoy schlock movies because we don't always want gems.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1250981#post1250981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, it's not like anyone watched or enjoyed...[snip long list]</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of those are hardly gems (however enjoyable some of them are. But there's plenty of not great movies of a lot of those as well. Is the Disney animated Snow White a classic? Sure. Are there a bunch of turds both animated and live action from the rest of the public domain world? Yeah.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Disney has consistently proven that the public domain can be a great source of cinematic inspiration. It's actually rather frustrating that they've strangled it so thoroughly after exploiting it so consistently. </div> </div> </div>But as you mention, Disney also loves to try to monopolize stories... even public domain ones, so we don't see a gigantic list of Sleeping Beauty movies to compare to theirs.<br /> <br /> How many of the movies you mentioned have a ton of competition despite being public domain? Their public domain status was more, &quot;Disney managed to sit on it,&quot; rather than them being open to lots of people making movies and lots of gems coming out of the process. This is especially true because Disney's history is full of stories that don't exactly work well as franchises like Star Wars (the sequels to most of the Disney animated canon are... not so good).<br /> <br /> Despite Disney's efforts, there aren't exactly a lot of Aladdin movies to make after Aladdin that are worth doing. The Aladdin world isn't worth expanding on. Etc. What's everyone else supposed to do besides try to copy the existing movie; maybe with some twist that usually ends up turning people off.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the sheer dearth we have of stuff that's been added to the public domain in recent years (thanks in no small part to Disney pushing for the laws about when things can the public domain being changed) makes these kinds of assumptions a bit iffy. </div> </div> </div>It might not be the perfect evidence, but we have a plethora of public domain films made from things far too old for copyrighting to look at.<br /> <br /> Even the few examples of public domain recent properties aren't encouraging. The Night of the Living Dead being public domain didn't lead to a huge number of gem &quot;Night of...&quot; films. There's plenty of good zombie movies out there, but most of them didn't need the first major modern zombie movie to be public domain to exist beyond maybe all the turds saturating horror films to make the genre tropes common and well defined.<br /> <br /> Of course, part of the problem is that the list of US made films that were allowed to lapse into the public domain is pretty short. Roger Corman generally didn't bother renewing his, but how many people are thinking there's a cash cow if redoing Corman movies anyway?<br /> <br /> Basically, while the evidence against might be sparse... at least it exists. There isn't really evidence for letting Star Wars go public domain as a good thing for future films.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-03T11:40:46-07:00","id":1251127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1250571#post1250571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Ok, I have to comment on this.<br /> <br /> One, in the old EU, the Star Wars universe was technologically stagnant. They'd had hyperdrive technology for thousands of a years. Why in 30 years would technology need to advance? Especially under the rule of the Empire? 30 years in a spacefairing society is nothing. Why wouldn't the same ships still be in use? Granted, that was the old EU, but I'd still think in the new cannon that idea that Galaxy is technological stagnant still holds true.<br /> <br /> To that point, and for a real world equivalent, this video summed it up nicely:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=p4zU-90QbvE\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=p4zU-90QbvE</a></div> </div> </div> </div>And that sums up the problem precisely to my point ...<br /> <br /> If you are the Galactic Superpower, attempting to stay ahead of the curve Technologically, then you do not want to maintain a static status quo --- Especially, if you are Changing the Guard, from the Empire to the First Order. Two separate super powers.<br /> <br /> Take the video you posted for example ... This guy says the military was using the same model of Helicopter from 1979. Okay, great. That is fine because he is talking about the same Country.<br /> <br /> If a New World Government came in to take over the United States, one that is 30 years advanced in Tech, they would not be using Helicopters from 1979. And, they would have New Tech included, not available from 1979.<br /> <br /> To further that point ... Take the Auto Maker, Jeep --- Most of their vehicles have maintained the same shape throughout the decades. Just look at the Jeep Wrangler and you'll know what I'm talking about.<br /> <br /> The Jeep Renegade also shared this same basic frame work --- That is, until Jeep merged with Fiat and now the Jeep Renegade's body structure has changed as the first Crossbreed Vehicle between the two Auto Companies --- The Renegade has all of the Modern Jeep Technology, with a Sportier Fiat body.<br /> <br /> Also true ... The US isn't trying to deploy these Helicopters into terrain different in observational perspective. When talking about Galaxy Wide, you are speaking of vast places New Tech would need to be implemented in, because in 30 years, there is no way the Galactic Military hasn't been exposed to previously unfamiliar Spacial detriments that would force them to restructure battle cruisers that would traverse the Galaxy after an upstart militant group who hideout in the fringes of the cosmos.<br /> <br /> To believe &quot;<i><b>That</b></i>&quot; is downright gullibility.<br /> <br /> .<br /> .<br /> .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6040,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6040-quiet-storm","user":"Quiet Storm","date":". 09-03-2018, 02:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6040-quiet-storm","name":"Quiet Storm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-03T14:29:15-07:00","id":1251184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quiet Storm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1251127#post1251127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that sums up the problem precisely to my point ...<br /> <br /> If you are the Galactic Superpower, attempting to stay ahead of the curve Technologically, then you do not want to maintain a static status quo --- Especially, if you are Changing the Guard, from the Empire to the First Order. Two separate super powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>To say again...the Star Wars universe seems to be technologically stagnant. They've had hyperdrive technology for thousands of years apparently. Why would technology need to change, especially in such a short span of time? Doesn't matter who is in charge of the galaxy...once you've reached the peak of technology there is no where to go.<br /> <br /> <br /> I understand what you're saying, and it applies perfectly to our current world and makes perfect sense. But the Star Wars universe had this kind of technology for thousands of years and they've encountered every type of world and environment possible long before the Empire came into power. There is basically no new technology to invent. Sure, the external hulls of ships appears the change from time to time, but the internal workings appear to basically be the same.<br /> <br /> So what I'm trying to say is, while 30 years in a long time for technology to change and evolve in our current world, that isn't the case in the Star Wars universe. At least that's the way it looks to me.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ran across this, which talks a bit about why technology in star wars never changes. Thought I'd share:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/pnY7Pak11tg?t=138\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/pnY7Pak11tg?t=138\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/pnY7Pak11tg?t=138\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/pnY7Pak11tg?t=138 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It should jump to about 2:18 in, but if not, skip to there to avoid the ad. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":24,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","user":"Mr Gone","date":". 09-03-2018, 05:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-03T15:10:14-07:00","id":1251195,"title":"","content":"Naw, I disagree.<br /> <br /> Basing that technology is at its peak because you've reach Hyperdrive is pretty limiting in and of itself. If Hyperdrive was the end al be all of Technology, then there is nothing else to build towards --- O' Wait, but the Death Star Cannon was only built around the time of Rogue One --- Hyperdrive as the ends to an technological future doesn't answer any of those questions. Because a technology that is Thousands of years old is over a Thousand years out dated.<br /> <br /> .<br /> .<br /> .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6040-quiet-storm","name":"Quiet Storm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-03T17:36:42-07:00","id":1251243,"title":"","content":"It's a silly sci-fi franchise build around the Rule of Cool rather than anything else, and if you've ever played the games or read the comics or novels about the Old Republic, which was 10,000 years before A New Hope, it all basically had the same kind of technology that you'll find in the Star Wars movies. So if you're mad about technology not progressing in ~30 years the fact that technology hadn't really changed much in 10,030 years would probably make your head explode.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-03T20:56:54-07:00","id":1251269,"title":"","content":"And you know, Star Wars was always less science-fiction and more science-fantasy.<br /> <br /> You want a long running franchise that slides a bit more towards hard science-fiction, Star Trek is over thataway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-03T22:54:56-07:00","id":1251280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quiet Storm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1251195#post1251195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Naw, I disagree.<br /> .<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, you can disagree all you want, it's pretty fucking clear that Star Wars is technologically stunted. You can disagree if you want, but that makes you wrong, not equally valid.<br /> <br /> EDIT: also, as regards the idea of public domain, if you hate the new Star Wars, you will <i>hate</i> what happens if Star Wars becomes public domain. THat is the quickest way to redefine how bad Star Wars could get.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-04-2018, 02:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-03T23:33:49-07:00","id":1251289,"title":"","content":"To be fair, technology <i>has</i> appreciably advanced in Star Wars cannon. That\u2019s why the Resistance was surprised the First Order was able to track them through hyperspace. That\u2019s why the destructive capabilities of the Death Star and the Starkiller were unprecedented in their respective times. That\u2019s why the visual design of ships has changed over the course of the saga. Progress happens, it\u2019s just <i>incredibly slow</i> compared to real life. We can argue about whether or not that\u2019s realistic, but realistic or not, it is a fact of the setting, and has been since long before Disney took the reins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T01:03:34-07:00","id":1251306,"title":"","content":"&quot;Incredibly slow compared to real life,&quot; isn't even that accurate. We've all grown up in a period of massive technological advance. 30 years of fairly limited development feels stagnant to us, but over the course of history that's pretty much status quo. Right now, trying to innovate is a goal to pursue, because we know we haven't tapped the current potential of many technologies, but over history lots of things were invented multiple times because someone figured it out before there was a practical way to make it happen.<br /> <br /> We also have technologies we basically haven't changed in thousands of years. Maybe improved on, or meshed with new technologies, but a magnetic compass basically works the same today as it did 2,000 years ago. We have fancy ones to work in our smart phones... but it's the same exactly principle designed for a computer instead of a human eye to read.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T06:59:09-07:00","id":1251378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1251289#post1251289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That\u2019s why the visual design of ships has changed over the course of the saga. Progress happens, it\u2019s just <i>incredibly slow</i> compared to real life.</div> </div> </div> </div>This puts me in mind of how, in real life, not all progress has equal flash.<br /> <br /> For example, motor cars basically follow the same precepts now as they did about a hundred years ago, even if there are all kinds of subtle improvements to performance and functionality, fuel efficiency and emissions. We're starting to take tentative steps into the realms of electric and self-driving cars, but that's still a far cry from the 1950s expectation that we'd have magic hovercars by now.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T10:50:13-07:00","id":1251437,"title":"","content":"Let's be honest and admit Star Wars tech was more or less stayed the same because of brand recognition. If things change to much technologically it won't be Star Wars anymore in a lot of fans minds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T12:15:00-07:00","id":1251459,"title":"","content":"Not sure how much of it actually is Star Wars anymore.<br /> <br /> .<br /> .<br /> .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6040-quiet-storm","name":"Quiet Storm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T12:20:09-07:00","id":1251460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1251280#post1251280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, you can disagree all you want, it's pretty fucking clear that Star Wars is technologically stunted. You can disagree if you want, but that makes you wrong, not equally valid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, you can see where in the actual movies they talk about technology advancements, and realize that your comment is absolutely illegitimate.<br /> <br /> .<br /> .<br /> .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6040-quiet-storm","name":"Quiet Storm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T14:57:40-07:00","id":1251500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quiet Storm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1251460#post1251460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or, you can see where in the actual movies they talk about technology advancements, and realize that your comment is absolutely illegitimate.<br /> <br /> .<br /> .<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Cited quotes please, or no buy.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T15:39:47-07:00","id":1251510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quiet Storm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1251460#post1251460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or, you can see where in the actual movies they talk about technology advancements, and realize that your comment is absolutely illegitimate.<br /> <br /> .<br /> .<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey man, you started the show with this argument, you're the ringleader here- we're just the audience calling bullshit. Them citations is on you, not the other way around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-05T04:36:19-07:00","id":1251614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quiet Storm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1251195#post1251195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Naw, I disagree.<br /> <br /> Basing that technology is at its peak because you've reach Hyperdrive is pretty limiting in and of itself. If Hyperdrive was the end al be all of Technology, then there is nothing else to build towards --- O' Wait, but the Death Star Cannon was only built around the time of Rogue One --- Hyperdrive as the ends to an technological future doesn't answer any of those questions. Because a technology that is Thousands of years old is over a Thousand years out dated.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say they reached the peak with the Hyperdrive. I just said they've had the Hyperdrive for thousands of years...and they seem to have reached the peak of technology.<br /> <br /> The Deathstar is just a giant laser. It's not new, per se, it's just big.<br /> <br /> And I'm not saying there can't be new technology in the Star wars universe, just that they seemed to be at the pinnacle, technology wise. Technology advancements would happen sloooooow in the Star Wars universe. They just don't have the need for anything truly new. Right?<br /> <br /> <br /> These guys get it:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1251306#post1251306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Incredibly slow compared to real life,&quot; isn't even that accurate. We've all grown up in a period of massive technological advance. 30 years of fairly limited development feels stagnant to us, but over the course of history that's pretty much status quo. Right now, trying to innovate is a goal to pursue, because we know we haven't tapped the current potential of many technologies, but over history lots of things were invented multiple times because someone figured it out before there was a practical way to make it happen.<br /> <br /> We also have technologies we basically haven't changed in thousands of years. Maybe improved on, or meshed with new technologies, but a magnetic compass basically works the same today as it did 2,000 years ago. We have fancy ones to work in our smart phones... but it's the same exactly principle designed for a computer instead of a human eye to read.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1251378#post1251378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This puts me in mind of how, in real life, not all progress has equal flash.<br /> <br /> For example, motor cars basically follow the same precepts now as they did about a hundred years ago, even if there are all kinds of subtle improvements to performance and functionality, fuel efficiency and emissions. We're starting to take tentative steps into the realms of electric and self-driving cars, but that's still a far cry from the 1950s expectation that we'd have magic hovercars by now.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1251289#post1251289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, technology <i>has</i> appreciably advanced in Star Wars cannon. That\u2019s why the Resistance was surprised the First Order was able to track them through hyperspace. That\u2019s why the destructive capabilities of the Death Star and the Starkiller were unprecedented in their respective times. That\u2019s why the visual design of ships has changed over the course of the saga. Progress happens, it\u2019s just <i>incredibly slow</i> compared to real life. We can argue about whether or not that\u2019s realistic, but realistic or not, it is a fact of the setting, and has been since long before Disney took the reins.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a good point too. Advancements do happen, just over a long period. Where as we make advancements seemingly every day, there just isn't the need in the Star Wars universe.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-05T16:52:33-07:00","id":1251788,"title":"","content":"Here's a question for people. If you think the tech seems too similar to the previous movies, what would you have liked to see? I'm just curious to hear what peoples idea's would be for how the tech should have changed in the 30 years between the two trilogies....<br /> <br /> BTW, if the Rian Johnson trilogy still happens, a brand new aesthetic is something I'm kind of looking forward to. Don't get me wrong, I love the current look of the Star Wars movies, but it'll be cool to see something brand new(ish).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-09T16:42:13-07:00","id":1252868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=w1VeOlIDD9o\" data-code=\"w1VeOlIDD9o\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/w1VeOlIDD9o/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Thought this was pretty good. But, I like that guys channel..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T08:35:54-07:00","id":1253075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AOESuLUOk6g\" data-code=\"AOESuLUOk6g\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/AOESuLUOk6g/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> If you have the time, I thought this was a really good video as well...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T17:02:46-07:00","id":1253163,"title":"","content":"I may be courting controversy here, but the Pop Culture Detective makes fantastic videos analyzing lots of popular media, and in particular how they portray masculinity. He did one on TLJ. You probably won\u2019t like it if you don\u2019t like hearing that sexism plays a major role in the hate for TLJ though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T18:59:51-07:00","id":1253185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1253163#post1253163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You probably won\u2019t like it if you don\u2019t like hearing that sexism plays a major role in the hate for TLJ though.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's his argument in a nutshell? The video is about 20 minutes long and I don't have time to watch it any time soon. I know at least in this thread we've seen a number of arguments from various people about why they think TLJ is a crummy movie and off-hand I can't recall sexism playing a role in any of them. Rather most of the hate I've seen directed towards TLJ revolves around the poor writing, poor resolutions, poor plot points, etc.<br /> <br /> For example some people think that TLJ throwing out many of the plot points and build up from TFA was wonderful and it was better for Johnson to ignore what Abrams had set up in the first movie than to build on top of it. Other people think that was a terrible decision and that it really ended up seriously hurting the new trilogy. I'm not sure that sexism has much of anything to do with that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T19:37:56-07:00","id":1253195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1251510#post1251510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey man, you started the show with this argument, you're the ringleader here- we're just the audience calling bullshit. Them citations is on you, not the other way around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, when you say things are Bullshit. And are merely jumping on someone else's coat tails to drive your point, that is on you. You want specifics from me ... Why, when I have already mentioned some that you chose so obviously to ignore ..?<br /> <br /> Yes, The Death Star is a different sort of Tech that was not previously used. Remember, Episode IV was made in the 70's, but the Story happens later. The Death Star Cannon [which I apparently have to mention again] Was a jump in Technology, and, whether You Paid Attention or not ... Was the entire Plot of Rouge One.<br /> <br /> Lightsabres now being Forked, rather than just one straight stream, or double ended.<br /> <br /> And as someone else pointed out after my original post, They chased the rebels by tracking them through Hyperspace Trails, which was mentioned directly in The Last Jedi as being an undeveloped technology.<br /> <br /> But hey, those things which were Major Plot points of the Movies that dealt with Tech development. I guess, when I say just watch the Movies, it's because from your comments, you probably hadn't.<br /> <br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6040-quiet-storm","name":"Quiet Storm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T22:28:23-07:00","id":1253218,"title":"","content":"Nobody's saying that all technological development in the Star Wars universe stopped. We're saying that the rate of advancement is fair slow due to technological limits being hit in a large number of fields, and the inertia of any military-industrial complex (that is, if you have a Star Destroyer factory already, it's much easier to retrofit existing Star Destroyers and build knew ones with updated packages, than it is to build an entirely new ship design, the new factories with it, and stop using Star Destroyers completely).<br /> <br /> None of the developments you've mentioned represent innovations that would drastically impact what spaceship designs would actually look like. The Death Star? It's a giant beam weapon that needs a station as big as a moon to operate. You're not going to redesign TIE Fighters because of it. A forked lightsabre? Nothing indicates this is actually new tech (forking plasma and energy is something we can do IRL), and nothing even really shows it's all that practical or beneficial. Only one person is using it. New tracking tech? No reason to redesign the entire ship, it's just a new sensor package.<br /> <br /> The complaint is, &quot;why are they using ships from 30 years ago, instead of brand new ships?&quot; which some technological developments that don't have any impact of ship design doesn't address.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T04:15:15-07:00","id":1253249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1253163#post1253163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may be courting controversy here, but the Pop Culture Detective makes fantastic videos analyzing lots of popular media, and in particular how they portray masculinity. He did one on TLJ. You probably won\u2019t like it if you don\u2019t like hearing that sexism plays a major role in the hate for TLJ though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I saw that! I really like that channel and enjoyed that video.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T04:26:56-07:00","id":1253251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1253185#post1253185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example some people think that TLJ throwing out many of the plot points and build up from TFA was wonderful and it was better for Johnson to ignore what Abrams had set up in the first movie than to build on top of it. Other people think that was a terrible decision and that it really ended up seriously hurting the new trilogy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry to just pick out this one bit(The sexism bit is a complaint I've seen on the internet, but not necessarily here), but I think it could be argued that Rian Johnson didn't throw out Abrams plot points, but did just about the only thing he could with them. I mean, Luke was hiding on that island and didn't come help Han or the Resistance for what reason? For me, what Johnson did made perfectly logical sense.<br /> <br /> Anyway, some of this is addressed in the videos I posted.<br /> <br /> Though, now that I'm typing this, what other plot points did Abrams leave hanging that Johnson supposedly ignored? I'm drawing a blank? Rey Parentage? I'll admit there was a line in TFA that might lead people to believe she was related to Luke. But that wouldn't have made any sense really...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T06:25:33-07:00","id":1253270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1253251#post1253251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry to just pick out this one bit(The sexism bit is a complaint I've seen on the internet, but not necessarily here), but I think it could be argued that Rian Johnson didn't throw out Abrams plot points, but did just about the only thing he could with them. I mean, Luke was hiding on that island and didn't come help Han or the Resistance for what reason? For me, what Johnson did made perfectly logical sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, during the opening crawl of The Force Awakens it set up with the premise that the First Order was hunting Luke down - that their first and primary goal was to kill him. So the assumption was that he had gone &quot;underground&quot; in order to keep out of sight and fight back. There was also Han's mention that Luke had gone to the first Jedi Temple, so there was lots of speculation that he had gone there to cultivate his mastery of the Force, learn some new secret techniques, to do research on the enemy (the Knights of Ren implying that there was a group of evil Force users), to set up a new school for Force users, etc.<br /> <br /> Basically that whatever he was doing was important - important enough that he left his friends, but at the same time he also left a map to his location so they could come get him if things got bad enough. Additionally he split up the map to make it harder for the First Order to track him down.<br /> <br /> Which is why Johnson's idea that Luke just wanted to go off to the far ends of the galaxy to die alone and didn't want anyone to find him doesn't really make a lot of sense. People who go into hiding because they don't want anyone to find them generally don't create puzzle maps pinpointing the exact location where they'll be so as to make it easy for people to come find them. That would defeat the entire purpose.<br /> <br /> On sexism I hang out in various nerdspaces on the internet where Star Wars eventually comes up, and once it does people start talking about TLJ. I've seen people call Rey a shallow character (which I'd agree with) or a Mary Sue (which I wouldn't but then there isn't a firm definition of what a Mary Sue is and Rey has some of the elements typically associated with one) but I haven't seen too many arguments that are rooted in sexism, certainly not to the point where I'd agree off hand that sexism plays a major role (or even a somewhat out-sized role) in the hate that TLJ gets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 09-11-2018, 12:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T11:47:57-07:00","id":1253335,"title":"","content":"The thing about predjudice, sexism included, is that it\u2019s pernicious. Very, very few people consciously dislike TLJ because they hate women and hate seeing women in prominent roles in the film (and even fewer of them would admit it.) However, most of the world is built with male-centric bias. Our baseline expectations about gender relations are informed by our cultural norms, which are rooted in a lot of biases and predjudice. So you may not think \u201cI don\u2019t like Rey/Admiral Holdo/Rose/Rian Johnson\u2019s depiction of Leia/etc. because they are women who excercize authority over men and that makes me uncomfortable,\u201d that doesn\u2019t mean it isn\u2019t the case.<br /> <br /> The thesis of the Pop Culture Detective\u2019s video is that The Last Jedi is all about subverting expectations, not only of the story of Star Wars, but of the space fantasy genre, and especially of the lone hero narrative and the view of masculinity it presents. The idea that a significant part of the hate for the film comes from people who are unfomfotable seeing the characters they expect to be archetypal masculine heroes being challenged by women is really just a side-note to his argument, necessary because it\u2019s a big part of the discourse surrounding TLJ, but not necessary to support his thesis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T12:51:42-07:00","id":1253356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1253335#post1253335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The idea that a significant part of the hate for the film comes from people who are unfomfotable seeing the characters they expect to be archetypal masculine heroes being challenged by women is really just a side-note to his argument, necessary because it\u2019s a big part of the discourse surrounding TLJ, but not necessary to support his thesis.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was big in Breaking Bad. Though Skye was put on a more antagonistic track to begin with. It's big everywhere, really, which I guess is why it's so ingrained.<br /> <br /> It's weird how if you have a male protagonist, their female 'support' characters, wives, coworkers, whatever, tend to be treated as obstacles to overcome. Even in base sitcoms, plots are often about a guy trying to do something their wife or girlfriend doesn't want them to do. That's them both being strong or independent. But if you have a female character who, say, like Samwise Gamgee, just follows the main character around rooting for them, they're sort of dismissed as an empty character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T17:27:04-07:00","id":1253426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1253270#post1253270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've seen people call Rey a shallow character (which I'd agree with) or a Mary Sue (which I wouldn't but then there isn't a firm definition of what a Mary Sue is and Rey has some of the elements typically associated with one) but I haven't seen too many arguments that are rooted in sexism</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026Are you sure you haven't?<br /> <br /> Or rather, is Rey any more of a shallow character than Luke Skywalker was in his heyday? Is there not perhaps a bias that is presented by where people set the tolerance threshold?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T19:19:36-07:00","id":1253456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1253270#post1253270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, during the opening crawl of The Force Awakens it set up with the premise that the First Order was hunting Luke down - that their first and primary goal was to kill him. So the assumption was that he had gone &quot;underground&quot; in order to keep out of sight and fight back. There was also Han's mention that Luke had gone to the first Jedi Temple, so there was lots of speculation that he had gone there to cultivate his mastery of the Force, learn some new secret techniques, to do research on the enemy (the Knights of Ren implying that there was a group of evil Force users), to set up a new school for Force users, etc.<br /> <br /> Basically that whatever he was doing was important - important enough that he left his friends, but at the same time he also left a map to his location so they could come get him if things got bad enough. Additionally he split up the map to make it harder for the First Order to track him down.<br /> <br /> Which is why Johnson's idea that Luke just wanted to go off to the far ends of the galaxy to die alone and didn't want anyone to find him doesn't really make a lot of sense. People who go into hiding because they don't want anyone to find them generally don't create puzzle maps pinpointing the exact location where they'll be so as to make it easy for people to come find them. That would defeat the entire purpose.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess my first question would be, was it Luke who split up the map? Or the one who left a map to his location? I could make some argument's that it wasn't...<br /> <br /> But, if Luke went into hiding to &quot;cultivate his mastery of the Force&quot;, why would he let Han die? Or let the Republic be destroyed? If he was building up his Force power, shouldn't he have seen what might happen and work to stop it?<br /> <br /> So, there had to be some reason why he wouldn't show up.<br /> <br /> Also, While not totally related, this video makes some good points about Luke and why his character may have been written the way he was in this movie:<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bxDX-nywiTc\" data-code=\"bxDX-nywiTc\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/bxDX-nywiTc/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Skip to about 9:42 to hear about how Luke is related to other mythological characters...<br /> <br /> Anyway, I can concede the point that there was a lot of way to read into TFA as to why Luke had vanished. But, as you mentioned, a lot of that was speculation.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T19:19:53-07:00","id":1253457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1253426#post1253426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or rather, is Rey any more of a shallow character than Luke Skywalker was in his heyday? Is there not perhaps a bias that is presented by where people set the tolerance threshold?</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought Luke during Episode 4 was pretty interesting. He had the the whole issue with his adopted family and wanting to get treated like an adult, then them getting killed, his desire for revenge, his trying to compete with Han, his training with scenes with Obi-wan, Luke developed a lot over the course of the first movie to become a more mature person than he had been at the beginning. That was, to a large degree, the entire point of the movie. And the second movie really pushed his character development with the Rebellion's defeat, his training with Yoda, his decision to abandon his training, finding out he was Darth Vader's son, etc. Sure we can say his story was a little generic in retrospect but as a character we got a lot of various looks at him, his emotions and his desires as the movies progressed.<br /> <br /> Just to note I had a similar problem with Anakin Skywalker in the prequel movies, with him being rather shallow, feeling too two-dimensional as a character and what development he got was often pretty poor. I'd imagine that a lot of the people who were unhappy with Rey also weren't too thrilled with Anakin for many of the same reasons. And I don't remember many arguments involving the prequels suggesting that people's dislike for Anakin as a character was due more to sexism rather than simply due to poor writing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 09-11-2018, 10:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T19:57:57-07:00","id":1253459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1253457#post1253457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought Luke during Episode 4 was pretty interesting. He had the the whole issue with his adopted family and wanting to get treated like an adult, then them getting killed, his desire for revenge, his trying to compete with Han, his training with scenes with Obi-wan, Luke developed a lot over the course of the first movie to become a more mature person than he had been at the beginning. That was, to a large degree, the entire point of the movie. And the second movie really pushed his character development with the Rebellion's defeat, his training with Yoda, his decision to abandon his training, finding out he was Darth Vader's son, etc. Sure we can say his story was a little generic in retrospect but as a character we got a lot of various looks at him, his emotions and his desires as the movies progressed.</div> </div> </div> </div>And we can say that Rey has a whole thing in which she's needed to adapt and survive in a harsh and abusive environment that she was abandoned in, creating a combination of a certain guardedness and wide-eyed, sheltered idealism, which has led to things like a strong need to belong somewhere and be part of something, seen most acutely in starting to adopt Han Solo (another perennial outsider) as a parental figure. <br /> <br /> Depending on the priorities of the observer.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T20:30:51-07:00","id":1253467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1253459#post1253459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And we can say that Rey has a whole thing in which she's needed to adapt and survive in a harsh and abusive environment that she was abandoned in, creating a combination of a certain guardedness and wide-eyed, sheltered idealism, which has led to things like a strong need to belong somewhere and be part of something, seen most acutely in starting to adopt Han Solo (another perennial outsider) as a parental figure.</div> </div> </div> </div>By the end of the second movie she doesn't feel much different from how she started at the beginning of the start of the first movie. In contrast Finn's had a good amount of character development and feels like he's come a way from who he started out as. Kylo Renn also feels like he's grown a bit. But it feels like Rey generally hasn't had that kind of character growth. If sexism is an issue then maybe part of it is with the script not giving her the kind of character growth we're seeing in the male characters?<br /> <br /> I had a big moment of excitement when she went into the Dark Force cave, hoping we'd see a vision that would show what was in store for her or push her character like we saw in Episode V when Luke entered the dark force cave, killed Vader and then saw his own face under the mask. But Rey's revelation in the cave was just... boring.<br /> <br /> The big thing I'm curious about is whether or not she stole the Jedi books before she left Luke or if Yoda just put them on the Falcon. Depending on the answer it might make her a bit more interesting as a character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 09-11-2018, 11:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T21:07:55-07:00","id":1253473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1253467#post1253467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By the end of the second movie she doesn't feel much different from how she started at the beginning of the start of the first movie.</div> </div> </div> </div>I must have missed the part of the beginning of the first movie in which she levitated a whole bunch of rocks.<br /> <br /> I think it's more productive to compare where she is at the end of the second movie with where she is at the end of the first one, since it's at that point of the first movie that we've effectively learned things about her and seen a number of impressions and relationships form that will change over the course of the second movie.<br /> <br /> (Also because the assertion that she's not changed since the start of the first movie is complete nonsense on the most simple basis of everything that happens to her across the films)<br /> <br /> So: at the end of the first movie, Rey is in a position of<br /> <br /> * Having been given an impression that there's something profound and mystical about her missing parents, whom she has always maintained intend to come back for her.<br /> * Extremely pissed off at Kylo Ren, whom she views as a brutal agent of the machine and a patricidal lunatic (not helped by him having killed somebody that she was starting to adopt as a surrogate father figure).<br /> * Only just starting to become aware of her sensitivity to the Force, taking her first tentative steps into a larger world.<br /> * Ready and eager to start learning from Luke Skywalker, who can probably serve as an alternative surrogate father figure, as well as somebody that she has already been established in the film to view with a mythic stature (she literally says that she thought he was a myth).<br /> <br /> By the end of the second movie, <i>every single one of these character points has undergone development</i>:<br /> <br /> * She's been forced to confront and accept the fact that her parents most likely abandoned her for a banal, even despicable reason, and will never again have any significance in her life. The time she spent dreaming that they would return for her has been wasted.<br /> * Her perception of Ren (whom she insistently addresses as Ben Solo) has become more nuanced, through a combination of learning things about his history with Luke, seeing the manner in which he was treated by Snoke, and personal conversations with him. She's transitioned from having very furiously trying to kill him to having fought at his side and saved his life! She's still in an antagonistic position to him, but she also thinks that he can be brought around, and has learned things from him*.<br /> * She's not only received some formal instruction in the Force, but had to go on a personal mystical journey to see more of it and learn more about her place therein. What is found there is not altogether positive, and that has some implications for her future. But she ends on a note of having grown stronger and more confident in her own power, and being in a position to continue learning.<br /> * Actually meeting Luke Skywalker causes him to fall from the pedestal a bit, both in terms of his general personality and lifestyle, and specifically learning about what happened between him and Ren. She learns from him and departs from him on a positive note, but still kind of ultimately rejects his validity as a mentor figure to her or anybody else.<br /> <br /> So Rey's arc across the two films can kind of be seen as a lost outsider who is really looking for a place and authoritative, even mythic figures to provide her with guidance and validation, through a process of finding and losing some of those and needing to deal with the impact, and ultimately into a general state of rejecting such hero worship while still being ready to try and glean what insight they provided so that she can seize and shape her own destiny.<br /> <br /> It would be a bit on the nose to quote Luke Skywalker directly, buuuuuutttt\u2026.<br /> <br /> * I admit, The Last Jedi was a film that was having difficulty getting a hook into me until we started getting exchanges between Rey and Kylo. I think it may be one of the most fascinating relationship dynamics in any Star Wars film.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If sexism is an issue then maybe part of it is with the script not giving her the kind of character growth we're seeing in the male characters?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or it could be in inherent bias that blinds a person to what actually happens in the film.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T04:29:36-07:00","id":1253545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1253467#post1253467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The big thing I'm curious about is whether or not she stole the Jedi books before she left Luke or if Yoda just put them on the Falcon. Depending on the answer it might make her a bit more interesting as a character.</div> </div> </div> </div>She absolutely stole those books. That's why Yoda had no issues burning down that tree. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T04:37:42-07:00","id":1253546,"title":"","content":"Oh...on the discussion of Luke and Rey, one of the videos I liked to earlier talks about Rey is in some ways of the opposite of Luke. Luke wanted to leave, while Rey wanted to stay. Things like that.<br /> <br /> After the first viewing of TFA, my son talked to me about how everyone was calling TFA a remake of ANH, and he thought while some things were similar, he thought a lot of the characters seemed like mirrors of the original characters. The above mentioned Rey wanting to stay while Luke wanted to leave, Kylo Ren feeling a pull to the light side while Vader dealt with his pull to the Dark, etc. I thought it was interesting...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T17:47:50-07:00","id":1253749,"title":"","content":"By the way, a possible point of consideration on how much people overlook Rey's character arc-<br /> <br /> While Levi described it way more marvelously then I did, I should point out that her arc has been spelled out several times in this thread, with even myself having provided a nutshell analysis of it.<br /> <br /> Now not everyone reads the whole thread-but if what Levi's said is new to you and you've been in here for quite a while....well, you might really be reading a clearly certain way and probably have reasons for it, but it pays to look closely at it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-15T18:11:23-07:00","id":1254660,"title":"","content":"I'm just after having watched The Last Jedi in full for the first time since I saw it in the cinema. I've got to say, it definitely feels like a stronger film for a second watch; the thematic thoroughlines are more apparent when you know where a bunch of them are going, and some things that I felt as though dragged the first time flowed more smoothly when I already knew the length of them.<br /> <br /> One thing that feels more important on repeat viewing? Everything to do with the casino planet. My brother (who has made a... not quite a career, but a dedicated intellectual pursuit with a platform) helped illustrate why to me: that it's important to Finn's arc, because it puts him in contact with things that help him to care about more than just Rey and basic survival and the desire to run away from things. Both in getting a perspective on injustices, and a foil in the form of Benicio Del Toro's character; a man who is also more focused on basic standards of survival, but is just more skeevy about it. As my brother put it, people who are dissatisfied with how he just leaves are missing the importance of how just leaving is what Finn is learning <i>not</i> to do.<br /> <br /> (Also, repeat viewing illustrates how Rose was absolutely right to stop him from crashing into that giant laser, because no way would that have accomplished anything)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-15T22:24:03-07:00","id":1254695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1254660#post1254660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing that feels more important on repeat viewing? Everything to do with the casino planet. My brother (who has made a... not quite a career, but a dedicated intellectual pursuit with a platform) helped illustrate why to me: that it's important to Finn's arc, because it puts him in contact with things that help him to care about more than just Rey and basic survival and the desire to run away from things. Both in getting a perspective on injustices, and a foil in the form of Benicio Del Toro's character; a man who is also more focused on basic standards of survival, but is just more skeevy about it. As my brother put it, people who are dissatisfied with how he just leaves are missing the importance of how just leaving is what Finn is learning <i>not</i> to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel the same way about the casino planet sidequest that I do about the episode of Stranger Things where Eleven goes to hang out with Eight and her gang. Absolutely important and wonderful for the development of the characters involved, and absolutely disruptive pacing for the overall narrative. I love what both achieved for the characters involved, but wish they both could have been achieved in a less disjointed way. Also, in TLJ\u2019s case, I could have done with a little less droid slapstick.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1254660#post1254660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Also, repeat viewing illustrates how Rose was absolutely right to stop him from crashing into that giant laser, because no way would that have accomplished anything)</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I didn\u2019t think that required a repeat viewing. Did people really think he would have accomplished anything with his \u201csacrifice\u201d if Rose hadn\u2019t saved him?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-16T07:56:10-07:00","id":1254768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1254660#post1254660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing that feels more important on repeat viewing? Everything to do with the casino planet. My brother (who has made a... not quite a career, but a dedicated intellectual pursuit with a platform) helped illustrate why to me: that it's important to Finn's arc, because it puts him in contact with things that help him to care about more than just Rey and basic survival and the desire to run away from things. Both in getting a perspective on injustices, and a foil in the form of Benicio Del Toro's character; a man who is also more focused on basic standards of survival, but is just more skeevy about it. As my brother put it, people who are dissatisfied with how he just leaves are missing the importance of how just leaving is what Finn is learning <i>not</i> to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally with you. I keep saying all this talk about it was pointless. I feel like people seemed to miss the point of it, and I can't quite figure out why. Seems fairly obvious to me. Theres a few parts that could be trimmed down maybe, but it's still a worthwhile plot thread for the movie.<br /> <br /> I recently saw a listing for a fan edit they were calling the &quot;Anti-Cringe&quot; cut, and reading their cut list made me cringe. The casino stuff being the main thing they cut out. I just don't get people sometimes...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1254660#post1254660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Also, repeat viewing illustrates how Rose was absolutely right to stop him from crashing into that giant laser, because no way would that have accomplished anything)</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1254695#post1254695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I didn\u2019t think that required a repeat viewing. Did people really think he would have accomplished anything with his \u201csacrifice\u201d if Rose hadn\u2019t saved him?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, think I've seen people say they thought he was going to sacrifice himself the way Holdo did and it totally would have worked and Rose robbed him of his noble sacrifice. I thought they made it pretty obvious that there was no way that would have worked...<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-16T12:20:28-07:00","id":1254819,"title":"","content":"All those sound more like the main reasons anyone would have to hate the movie<br /> <br /> I don't say that to get into such finer points of it being good or bad.<br /> <br /> But more like this movie is truly special in that it somehow accidentally found a way to do things that would really have no middle ground, just love or hate","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24473-willowfang","name":"Willowfang","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24473_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-16T12:43:49-07:00","id":1254826,"title":"","content":"It might just be me, because I have a general tendency to find things longer the first time I see them (clear knowledge that they're finite makes them feel quicker), but I didn't really feel pacing issues in that second viewing. It all felt nice and flowing.<br /> <br /> Really, it felt like a weird kind of director's cut to me, except where the only editing was in my perspective and receptivity.<br /> <br /> I said earlier that I was a bit dubious about the film until it reached the Ben/Rey stuff. In the moment, I think that took a sense of feeling &quot;where is this going&quot; that kept me from effectively engaging. When I see it with foreknowledge of where it's all going, the question doesn't distract, and I could more effectively lock in from the word go.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1254695#post1254695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I didn\u2019t think that required a repeat viewing. Did people really think he would have accomplished anything with his \u201csacrifice\u201d if Rose hadn\u2019t saved him?</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly don't remember my initial take. It's been buried under the presentation in the How It Should Have Ended video.<br /> <br /> And I like that show, and am not entirely sure that they were being serious. But its text of &quot;Rose is saving one person while risking the Resistance&quot; was in a spot long enough after having seen the film that I assumed it was how it effectively played there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-17T08:18:06-07:00","id":1255005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1254826#post1254826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might just be me, because I have a general tendency to find things longer the first time I see them (clear knowledge that they're finite makes them feel quicker), but I didn't really feel pacing issues in that second viewing. It all felt nice and flowing.<br /> <br /> Really, it felt like a weird kind of director's cut to me, except where the only editing was in my perspective and receptivity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting! I\u2019ve only seen it the once, so maybe I\u2019d have a similar experience watching it again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1254826#post1254826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I said earlier that I was a bit dubious about the film until it reached the Ben/Rey stuff. In the moment, I think that took a sense of feeling &amp;quot;where is this going&amp;quot; that kept me from effectively engaging. When I see it with foreknowledge of where it's all going, the question doesn't distract, and I could more effectively lock in from the word go.<br /> <br /> I honestly don't remember my initial take. It's been buried under the presentation in the How It Should Have Ended video.<br /> <br /> And I like that show, and am not entirely sure that they were being serious. But its text of &amp;quot;Rose is saving one person while risking the Resistance&amp;quot; was in a spot long enough after having seen the film that I assumed it was how it effectively played there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it makes sense that a lot of those moments would come across differently upon a second viewing. The film relied a lot on setting up expectations based on common genre conventions, and then breaking the expectations it set up. We expect the confident war hero leading a charge against a superior force in spite of warnings from his superior to be successful and his daring gambit to be celebrated. Instead, Leia slaps Poe in the face and demotes him. We expect when the General is wounded in action for command to pass to the hero, instead it passes to some purple haired woman we\u2019ve never seen before, and doesn\u2019t take the hero seriously. We expect the hero of the previous generation to be exceptionally powerful and to pass that power on to the hero of the new generation, instead he tosses the symbol of his own power aside and makes fun of the notion that he could solve the heroes\u2019 problems himself. We expect the secret mission to get the McGuffin that could save the plucky resistance fighters to save the day, but instead it makes matters worse. We expect the mutiny against the seemingly corrupt admiral who disrespected our hero to vindicate him, instead we find out Holdo had a good reason for everything she had been doing and Poe was the one in the wrong. So, by the time they set up Fin for a heroic sacrifice that would seemingly buy the resistance enough time to escape, I was ready for it not to go as genre conventions dictate, and I recognized the clear signs that his attempted sacrifice was folly.<br /> <br /> You know, writing that all out, I realize Luke\u2019s line that they played up in the advertising, \u201cThis is not going to go the way you think\u201d was very appropos in a lot of ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-21T14:02:48-07:00","id":1256222,"title":"","content":"Does the The Last Jedi still work as a film if you don't have these expectations that it wants to subvert? I'm asking the because I think a lot of people enjoyed the film because it did that and I don't think I was able to enjoy the film because it requires you to be amazed at it breaking genre conventions. <br /> <br /> Like for instance, I feel like the film wants me to be impressed that Finn and Rose were betrayed by the hacker character but watching the film I predicted that would happen because, well, the film flat out stated that this character was untrustworthy and only concerned about money, so when he betrayed our heroes when they got caught I was like &quot;Well, yeah. Why is anyone surprised that happened?&quot; <br /> <br /> This becomes a running problem in the film. Luke being a hermit that's given up is a subversion that seemed obvious to me because its the be only way to explain why Luke wasn't doing anything while the Empire 2.0 ravaged the galaxy. <br /> <br /> Rey's parents being nobodies and not Luke, Leia or a Kenobi was obvious to me because those fan theories were incredibly stupid and seemed to forget that Force-Sensitives don't have to come from ancient lineages. Rey won the genetic lottery and that's why she's so powerful. That's it. No other explanation needed. <br /> <br /> Kylo Ren sticking to the Dark Side was predictable to me because A) He's the central antagonist of the Sequel trilogy, not Snoke or Hux and B) He never said or did anything in The Last Jedi that made me believe he regretted being a Space Nazi. I mean, re-watching those Skype calls of his with Rey it seems obvious that he's still a monster and was just trying to manipulate Rey into killing Luke, right? So when he decided that he wanted to continue being a Space Nazi I was like &quot;Well, yeah.&quot; <br /> <br /> Poe's plan not working and getting everyone killed also wasn't a surprise because, well, his plan was obviously idiotic. The guy trusted a random engineer and a former foot solider to lead an infiltration mission on planet that's low-key supporting the First Order. And course, they make the dumbest decisions imaginable because they have absolutely no training for what they are about to do and only &quot;succeed&quot; because they had the random luck to be locked up with an ace hacker. That said, Poe suddenly being made the leader of the Resistance did surprise at the end of the film. I mean, the film had been logical so-far with making sure that obviously idiotic actions are punished, but after Poe gets several people killed twice and causes a mutiny he's awarded and given back his position of authority instead of being demoted forever. That was indeed quite the surprise. <br /> <br /> Anyways, I have other problems with the film but the idea that the subversion of tired tropes makes it good or interesting doesn't really make sense to me because I feel that if you came into the film without those expectations than the film loses its surprise and you're left with obvious things happening for obvious reasons. It also doesn't help that I think the tropes that The Last Jedi wants to subvert have already been subverted in other Star Wars films. I mean, the young flyboy thinking he can save the day by fighting someone or something has been done before. The same goes for the hero meeting a long-lost warrior that they thought was going to be their instructor but ultimately A) Doesn't want to train them initially and B) Isn't what they thought they would be has also been done before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-21T15:45:13-07:00","id":1256254,"title":"","content":"I think it would work without having those expectations, but it would take appreciating a different view of the film.<br /> <br /> Basically, TLJ is about a bunch of idealists (even Kylo and Poe would should know better by now) coming to grips with their idealism (or even naivety) and reality not lining up. These are characters that, in universe, largely grew up with some sanitized and romanticized version of the original trilogy fed to them. So all that stuff you see as, 'duh this would never work,' is supposed to be that way, but the characters don't know that yet. They're in the process of learning what you already know. The world isn't black and white, people don't change easily, tales of heroism skip all the stupidity and luck that makes the heroes look less good, etc.<br /> <br /> So yeah, if you saw all that coming? That's good, the point is the characters are evolving to understand things like you do. The movies are affirming your position by forcing the characters towards it so they can mature for the next one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-21T16:36:49-07:00","id":1256270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1256254#post1256254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it would work without having those expectations, but it would take appreciating a different view of the film.<br /> <br /> Basically, TLJ is about a bunch of idealists (even Kylo and Poe would should know better by now) coming to grips with their idealism (or even naivety) and reality not lining up. These are characters that, in universe, largely grew up with some sanitized and romanticized version of the original trilogy fed to them. So all that stuff you see as, 'duh this would never work,' is supposed to be that way, but the characters don't know that yet. They're in the process of learning what you already know. The world isn't black and white, people don't change easily, tales of heroism skip all the stupidity and luck that makes the heroes look less good, etc.<br /> <br /> So yeah, if you saw all that coming? That's good, the point is the characters are evolving to understand things like you do. The movies are affirming your position by forcing the characters towards it so they can mature for the next one.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I suppose I can understand how that can be enjoyable to watch, but I just found it tiresome being told things I already know. I guess I just would have perferred that the characters learned new things that I could learn with them instead of going over territory that's already been explored. But I don't think I should have expected that give that entire trilogy seems obsessed with the OT and literally took two films to finally break away from it. <br /> <br /> I do have to argue the point that morality isn't black-and-white in this film. While our heroes are shown to fail and make bad choices, ultimately were still supposed to see them as the protagonists and not question their goals. The Resistance is good and the First Order is bad and even the the Rebels 2.0 buying weapons from slavers is completely forgotten by the end of the film and Kylo Ren is still a Space Nazi leading an army of Space Nazis whose motivations are one-dimensional. Not that I want the Space Nazis &quot;to have a good point&quot; or anything, but if were really going to complicate the good vs evil paradigm than maybe our antagonists should be different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-21T16:49:35-07:00","id":1256274,"title":"","content":"By the &quot;world isn't black and white,&quot; I wasn't speaking strictly about the morality of the primary factions. There's a world beyond this conflict that isn't so simple, and narrative roles you were raised to believe in aren't that simple in reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-21T23:11:43-07:00","id":1256379,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t know, I wasn\u2019t surprised by the tropes being subverted either, I thought they were all sufficiently telegraphed. I was just pleasently surprised to see Star Wars under Disney subverting them, especially when the last one had been played so safe. My point wasn\u2019t that they were genuinely unexpected twists; quite the contrary, I was specifically responding with surprise to the people who missed the telegraphing and thought the movie had been trying to play those tropes straight, and musing that I imagine the movie would likely be a very different experience for them the second time around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-22-2018, 02:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-22T04:39:04-07:00","id":1256437,"title":"","content":"That's something I can confirm. I know of at least five people, myself included, who found the movie much better on the second watch.. In some cases they started out liking it and grew to think it was great. In some cases they started out really disliking it and grew to think it was good. In my case I enjoyed it a lot but thought it had serious flaws. Most of those flaws didn't seem like flaws on the second watch. Most.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T17:31:19-07:00","id":1256840,"title":"","content":"It's funny; the twist on the usual formula that I was so strongly expecting by about two-thirds into the film was that Rey actually would more wholly side with Kylo, and I was <b>so</b> on board with that and where it might go from there.<br /> <br /> I ultimately see that it's not really in her character, so I have no issue with it not going there, but I think it puts me on a slightly different wavelength than other people seeing telegraphed subversions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T17:38:40-07:00","id":1256841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1256840#post1256840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's funny; the twist on the usual formula that I was so strongly expecting by about two-thirds into the film was that Rey actually would more wholly side with Kylo, and I was <b>so</b> on board with that and where it might go from there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kylo Ren doesn't really seem to have a side, though, does he? He clearly wanted to kill Luke and others who stand against him, but he hasn't really demonstrated any goals or opinions about how the universe should work, has he?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T18:24:58-07:00","id":1256855,"title":"","content":"I mean, he has a side (his own), but you're right that as of the end of TLJ he doesn't really have grander plans or goals. But a big point of how things stand after Rey refuses to join him, and his final battle with Luke, is that he has to face that reality. He's fought very hard... and basically has gotten what he wanted (even if not how he wanted it) and now has no idea what to do with it since it didn't turn out like he thought it would. He's a dog that caught the car.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-24T04:51:07-07:00","id":1256931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1256855#post1256855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, he has a side (his own), but you're right that as of the end of TLJ he doesn't really have grander plans or goals. But a big point of how things stand after Rey refuses to join him, and his final battle with Luke, is that he has to face that reality. He's fought very hard... and basically has gotten what he wanted (even if not how he wanted it) and now has no idea what to do with it since it didn't turn out like he thought it would. He's a dog that caught the car.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Similarly, one of my favorite character moments in the movie is Hux's 'Oh shit' face as he sees Kylo raging at the end. That moment is such a breaking point for his character as he realizes there's no one else in charge anymore. No one to lead them. No one to give him the external validation he craves. No one to curry favor with. No one to control Kylo. Hux is the most capable person in the room now and it terrifies him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-27T20:03:38-07:00","id":1257707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1256841#post1256841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kylo Ren doesn't really seem to have a side, though, does he?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's... not really necessary to apply the phrase &quot;side with&quot;.<br /> <br /> Like, to side with his argument. Side with his personality. &quot;Hey, we're the only ones who can understand each other, let's stick together and figure out this crazy universe as we go&quot;. Not necessarily that he's got an organisation or fully developed ideology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-28T21:11:34-07:00","id":1257913,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/heat-vision/star-wars-chief-kathleen-kennedys-lucasfilm-deal-extended-three-years-1147653?utm_source=Sailthru&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_campaign=THR%20Breaking%20News_now_2018-09-28%2012:15:01_ehayden&amp;utm_term=hollywoodreporter_breakingnews\" target=\"_blank\">In other news, Kathleen Kennedy's contract as head of Lucasfilm has been renewed for another 3 years.</a><br /> <br /> Well, so much for &quot;fans&quot; being so self-assured that Kennedy was going to get fired...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-29T13:53:08-07:00","id":1258024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1257913#post1257913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/heat-vision/star-wars-chief-kathleen-kennedys-lucasfilm-deal-extended-three-years-1147653?utm_source=Sailthru&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_campaign=THR%20Breaking%20News_now_2018-09-28%2012:15:01_ehayden&amp;utm_term=hollywoodreporter_breakingnews\" target=\"_blank\">In other news, Kathleen Kennedy's contract as head of Lucasfilm has been renewed for another 3 years.</a><br /> <br /> Well, so much for &quot;fans&quot; being so self-assured that Kennedy was going to get fired...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why the hell would she? Because people didn't like the films she's produced and a cotton industry on YouTube complaining about her? So what? Pretty much all them with the exception of Solo made a shit ton of money. So as long as that continues her job is safe because that's just how capitalism works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-29T14:37:12-07:00","id":1258038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1258024#post1258024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Why the hell would she? Because people didn't like the films she's produced and a cotton industry on YouTube complaining about her? So what? Pretty much all them with the exception of Solo made a shit ton of money. So as long as that continues her job is safe because that's just how capitalism works.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess we will see with how well Episode IX does. that contract might not mean much if it does poorly at the box office.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-29T15:47:22-07:00","id":1258058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1258024#post1258024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why the hell would she? Because people didn't like the films she's produced and a cotton industry on YouTube complaining about her? So what? Pretty much all them with the exception of Solo made a shit ton of money. So as long as that continues her job is safe because that's just how capitalism works.</div> </div> </div> </div>I bring it up because, in the fever pitch of TLJ hatedom, there were rumors going around about how Disney execs weren't happy with Kennedy because of the divisive reception of TLJ and the poor box office of Solo. And among these rumors was that they were considering firing her from the position.<br /> <br /> Some of the hatedom YTers were running with this as absolute fact, and smugly declaring that they'll hear about Kennedy's resignation any day now, that it was victory for the &quot;true fans&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 09-29-2018, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-29T16:21:37-07:00","id":1258070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1167544-star-wars-the-last-jedi?p=1258058#post1258058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I bring it up because, in the fever pitch of TLJ hatedom, there were rumors going around about how Disney execs weren't happy with Kennedy because of the divisive reception of TLJ and the poor box office of Solo. And among these rumors was that they were considering firing her from the posit